# autoref — an automation reference reaches resolveAutomation, so every
# command accepts every identifier form the family prints (docs/decisions.md
# D-1; INVARIANTS.md H-17).
#
# A VIOLATION surface: internal/surfaceaudit.AutomationRefSurface lists only
# the run-entrypoints whose automation target never passes through the shared
# resolver — directly or via one of its one-hop wrappers
# (resolveAutomationConfigID, resolveAutomationEntityID, automationConfigIDFor).
# Empty is the goal, and it is empty. Guarded against silently matching nothing
# by TestAutomationRefExtractorFlagsAnUnresolvedTarget, which feeds the
# extractor a known-bad function.
#
# It was not empty. `auto rollback` matched the caller's reference against
# backup filenames, which `auto apply` keys by config id — so the object id
# `auto ls` prints, the entity_id and the alias all answered "no backup found
# for automation …" for an automation whose backup sat right there. The same
# mechanism had already produced issue #94's `auto diff`/`auto apply` defect:
# a parallel narrower lookup beside a resolver whose own doc comment named
# them as callers.
#ceiling 0
